From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi: Keep Assassin's Creed DX10 fullscreen on focus loss.

Assassin's Creed loses fullscreen presentation when switching to another
window. The local reproduction runs AssassinsCreed_Dx10.exe through DXVK.
Enable the existing dxgi.keepFullscreenOnFocusLoss compatibility option
for that executable, as already done for FFXIV and Black Desert.

This prevents DXGI's implicit focus-loss exit and focus-only occlusion
status. Explicit fullscreen/windowed requests, minimization and real input
focus are unchanged. Do not extend Black Desert's Wine activation-message
filter to this game without evidence that it is needed.

The profile matches the executable case-insensitively, including non-Steam
installs. The launcher and separate D3D9 executable are not affected.
Apply after black-desert-keep-fullscreen-on-focus-loss.patch.
Runtime verification is pending; no build was run when preparing this patch.

---
diff --git a/dxvk.conf b/dxvk.conf
--- a/dxvk.conf
+++ b/dxvk.conf
@@ -78,8 +78,9 @@
 # restore from dropping Wine's fullscreen upscaling. Focus and input still
 # belong to the newly activated window.
 # Explicit fullscreen/windowed requests and minimized-window handling remain
-# unchanged. This does not affect D3D9. Enabled by default for FFXIV and
-# Black Desert, which also needs Wine's application-deactivation fix.
+# unchanged. This does not affect D3D9. Enabled by default for FFXIV,
+# Assassin's Creed DX10 and Black Desert. Black Desert also needs Wine's
+# application-deactivation fix.
 #
 # Supported values: True, False
 
diff --git a/src/util/config/config.cpp b/src/util/config/config.cpp
--- a/src/util/config/config.cpp
+++ b/src/util/config/config.cpp
@@ -316,6 +316,10 @@
     { R"(\\AoE2DE_s\.exe$)", {{
       { "d3d11.cachedDynamicResources",        "a" },
     }} },
+    /* Assassin's Creed DX10: keep fullscreen when focus moves away. */
+    { R"(\\AssassinsCreed_Dx10\.exe$)", {{
+      { "dxgi.keepFullscreenOnFocusLoss",   "True" },
+    }} },
     /* Assassin's Creed 3 and 4                   */
     { R"(\\ac(3|4bf)[sm]p\.exe$)", {{
       { "d3d11.cachedDynamicResources",        "a" },
